[{"data":1,"prerenderedAt":111},["ShallowReactive",2],{"news-detail-daad-scholarship-funaab-2026-in-country-in-region-fully-funded-opportunity-118":3},{"news":4,"more":28},{"id":5,"slug":6,"title":7,"content":8,"authorName":9,"authorId":10,"status":11,"recommended":12,"datePosted":13,"deadline":14,"images":15,"notifiedAt":14,"notifiedBy":14,"createdAt":13,"updatedAt":21,"categories":22,"readTime":27},118,"daad-scholarship-funaab-2026-in-country-in-region-fully-funded-opportunity-118","Daad Scholarship Funaab 2026 (in-country\u002Fin-region): Fully Funded Opportunity","\u003Cp>DAAD Scholarship FUNAAB (Federal University of Agriculture Abeokuta): Fully Funded In-Country Opportunity\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>DAAD Scholarship FUNAAB Abstract\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Scholarship Host: DAAD\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Study Abroad: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarship\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study Abroad\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarship\u002Fscholarships-in-africa\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Study-In-Africa\u003C\u002Fa> \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Category: \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fpostgraduate-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Postgraduate Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fmasters-scholarships\u002F?utm_source=Google&amp;utm_medium=Catergory&amp;utm_campaign=Email+Campaign\">Masters Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa> || \u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fscholarships\u002Fphd-scholarships\u002F\">PhD Scholarships\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Benefits: Full Scholarship\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Tuition\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Accommodation\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>€8920 Living Stipends\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Travel &amp; Research Costs\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Eligibility: sub-Sahara African Countries\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Deadline: April 29, 2026\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>DAAD In-Country\u002FIn-Region Scholarship Details\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>The DAAD In-Country\u002FIn-Region Scholarships are granted for development-related Master or doctoral studies for individuals who plan to pursue a career in teaching and \u002F or research at a higher \u003Ca class=\"google-anno\" href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fscholarsworld.ng\u002Fdaad-scholarship-funaab\u002F#\"> \u003Cu>education\u003C\u002Fu>\u003C\u002Fa> institution in Sub-Saharan Africa.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>The programme aims to foster strong, internationally oriented higher education systems in Sub-Saharan Africa with the capacity to contribute to sustainable development.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>For this purpose, scholarships for development-related Master’s studies are awarded to individuals who plan to pursue a career in teaching and\u002For research at a higher education institution in Sub-Saharan Africa.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>By training future academic and professional leaders, the programme contributes to the following long-term impacts.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Qualified professionals’ involvement in the solution of development-related problems in Sub-Saharan Africa.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Graduates strengthening education and research in Sub-Saharan Africa.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Structural strengthening and regional networking of partner institutions and partner universities.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>DAAD Scholarship FUNAAB Benefits\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>The DAAD EPOS scholarship covers all fees related to study at the institution;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Tuition\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Living stipends €8920 (Accommodation, food, etc.)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Study and research allowance\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Thesis publishing costs\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>DAAD In-Country\u002FIn-Region Scholarship Requirements\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>To be eligible for the postgraduate DAAD In-Country\u002FIn-Region Scholarship, applicants must satisfy the following conditions:\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Applicants for a Master’s degree\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>graduates with a first academic degree, who have successfully completed a three-year university degree with above-average results (at least: Second-Class\u002FUpper Division or equivalent, if applicable)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Candidates who cannot provide a Second Class\u002FUpper Division or a higher result are not eligible\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>clearly show motivation and strong commitment;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>have a thorough knowledge of the language of instruction;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>have completed their last university degree not more than 6 years ago at the time of application;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>must be nationals or permanent residents of a Sub-Saharan African country\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Applicants for a PhD degree\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>postgraduates with a first academic degree, who have successfully\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>completed a two-year university Master’s degree (or equivalent) with above-average results (at least: Second Class\u002FUpper Division or equivalent, if applicable)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Candidates who cannot provide a Second Class\u002FUpper Division or a higher result are not eligible;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>\u003Cstrong>Required Documents for DAAD Scholarship FUNAAB (Federal University of Agriculture Abeokuta) 2026\u003C\u002Fstrong>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>While applying for the 2026 DAAD Scholarship FUNAAB, you will be required to submit the following documents;\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Complete DAAD Application Form\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Academic Transcripts\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>A full curriculum vitae in tabular form, if not otherwise possible without a signature\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>A list of publications (if applicable)\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>One Letter of recommendation form, filled, signed and stamped by a university lecturer\u002Fteacher. \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Letter of admission from the host institution\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Copies of university degree certificates including transcripts (if available) \u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>If the certificates are not in English or German, a certified translation must be submitted.\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003Cli>\u003Cp>Letter of motivation (1-2 pages with a personal, social motivation as well\u003Cbr \u002F>as a motivation for the studies and a possible Master project).\u003C\u002Fp>\u003C\u002Fli>\u003C\u002Ful>\u003Cp>APPLY HERE:\u003Ca href=\"https:\u002F\u002Fwww2.daad.de\u002Fdeutschland\u002Fstipendium\u002Fdatenbank\u002Fen\u002F21148-scholarship-database\u002F?detail=10000486\">https:\u002F\u002Fwww2.daad.de\u002Fdeutschland\u002Fstipendium\u002Fdatenbank\u002Fen\u002F21148-scholarship-database\u002F?detail=10000486\u003C\u002Fa>\u003C\u002Fp>\u003Cp>\u003C\u002Fp>","Linkskool",16,"published",0,"2026-04-07 09:19:19",null,[16],{"fileName":17,"oldFileName":17,"type":18,"file":19,"url":20},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdaad-scholarship-funaab-2026-in-country-in-region-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F69d4be07d1c612.13784898_screenshot 2026-04-07 090303.png","image","","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdaad-scholarship-funaab-2026-in-country-in-region-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F69d4be07d1c612.13784898_screenshot%202026-04-07%20090303.png","2026-06-24 11:55:43",[23],{"id":24,"name":25,"createdAt":26},2,"Opportunities","2026-01-07 13:35:07",3,[29,39,49,58,67,76,85,94,102],{"id":30,"slug":31,"title":32,"images":33,"datePosted":37,"authorName":38},305,"dartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity","Dartmouth College Kings Scholarship Usa 2026: Fully Funded Opportunity",[34],{"fileName":35,"oldFileName":35,"type":18,"file":19,"url":36},"assets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F6a3c3537be16a2.95289717_screenshot 2026-06-24 204255.png","https:\u002F\u002Flinkskool.com\u002Fassets\u002Felearning\u002Flrm\u002Fexplore\u002Fnews\u002Fdartmouth-college-kings-scholarship-usa-2026-fully-funded-opportunity\u002F6a3c3537be16a2.95289717_screenshot%202026-06-24%20204255.png","2026-06-24 20:51:19","LINKSKOOL",{"id":40,"slug":41,"title":42,"images":43,"datePosted":47,"authorName":48},304,"mexican-government-scholarship-for-foreigners-2026-fully-funded-opportunity","Mexican Government Scholarship For Foreigners 2026: Fully Funded Opportunity",[44],{"fileName":45,"oldFileName":45,"type":18,"file":19,"url":46},